# Blocks secret material headed for the PUBLIC repo tree.
#
# Two matchers, both scoped to files under $CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR (the repo —
# ~/.demo-builder project dirs and the scratchpad are legitimate .env /
# capture targets and stay untouched):
#   A. Write/Edit of any .env* file — secrets route through user-scoped VS
#      Code settings or SecretStorage, never tracked files.
#   B. Write/Edit whose CONTENT carries a high-confidence secret shape
#      (private-key block, GitHub/Slack/AWS/OpenAI-style token, credentialed
#      mongodb URI). Patterns are deliberately tight: the fake-test
#      convention (`fake-test-pw-not-a-secret`) and ordinary fixtures do not
#      match. Defense-in-depth beside GitGuardian, which scans only PR diffs
#      and is non-required on develop.
#
# NOT once-per-session (like 10-jest-pipe): a hard stop on publishing a
# secret must not be spendable.
rule_id=secret-files
rule_once=0

rule_match() {
    case "$1" in Write|Edit) ;; *) return 1 ;; esac
    [ -n "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR" ] || return 1     # fail open without a scope
    case "$3" in
        "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR"/*) ;;
        *) return 1 ;;                            # outside the repo — allowed
    esac

    # A. .env* basename
    case "${3##*/}" in
        .env|.env.*) return 0 ;;
    esac

    # B. high-confidence secret shapes in the content
    [ -n "$4" ] || return 1
    printf '%s' "$4" | grep -qE \
        -e '-----BEGIN [A-Z ]*PRIVATE KEY-----' \
        -e 'gh[ps]_[A-Za-z0-9]{30,}' \
        -e 'github_pat_[A-Za-z0-9_]{22,}' \
        -e 'AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}' \
        -e 'xox[baprs]-[0-9A-Za-z-]{10,}' \
        -e 'sk-(proj|ant)-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}' \
        -e 'mongodb(\+srv)?://[^:/[:space:]]+:[^@[:space:]]+@'
}

rule_message() {
    cat <<'MSG'
Blocked: this repo is PUBLIC (skukla/demo-builder-vscode) and the write targets its tree with secret material — a .env file or content matching a high-confidence secret pattern (private key, access token, credentialed connection string).
- Secrets route through user-scoped VS Code settings or SecretStorage, never tracked files.
- Test fixtures use the safe convention: fake-test-pw-not-a-secret.
- Real captures belong in the session scratchpad or ~/.demo-builder, not the repo.
If this is a false positive (e.g. documenting a pattern), rephrase the example so it no longer matches a real credential shape.
MSG
}
